<title>USA: Day Runner sets 600,000 share buyback.</title>
<headline>Day Runner sets 600,000 share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif. 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Day Runner Inc on Wednesday said its board of directors authorized a stock repurchase program of up to 600,000 of its common shares.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement the repurchases may take place from time to time on the open market and may be funded from cash flow.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe that this investment will be beneficial to both our stockholders and our company,&quot; said Mark Vidovich, Day Runner chairman and chief executive officer.</p>
<p>Shares in Day Runner, a maker of paper-based organizers for the retail market, closed down 3/4 at 23-3/8.</p>
</text>
